<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simon I of Kartli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1537">1537</a>–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simon I was King of Kartli in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> from 1556 to 1569 and again from 1578 to 1600. He resisted both Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, which held him captive for nearly a decade, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, fighting to keep his kingdom independent between them. Captured by the Ottomans in 1599, he died a prisoner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> in 1611.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-i-of-kartli.jpg" alt="Simon I of Kartli" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dominicus Custos · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Engraving_of_Simon_I_of_Kartli,_1600.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
